// Conway's Game of Life — toroidal board, two gliders and a pulsar.
//
// The board is a series of series of number: 0 is dead, 1 is alive.
// Every generation is a fresh board built from the neighbour counts of
// the previous one. Edges wrap.

Bind number to wrap-index, given (the number i, the number extent):
    If i is less than 1, return i + extent.
    If i is greater than extent, return i - extent.
    Return i.
Done.

Bind series of series of number to make-board, given (the number height, the number width):
    Define board as a series of series of number with ().
    For each r in range 1 to height, repeat:
        Define row as a series of number with ().
        For each c in range 1 to width, repeat:
            Add 0 to row.
        Done.
        Add row to board.
    Done.
    Return board.
Done.

Bind void to set-cell, given (the series of series of number board,
                              the number r, the number c,
                              the number height, the number width):
    Define rr as cast wrap-index on (r, height).
    Define cc as cast wrap-index on (c, width).
    Define row as item rr of board.
    The item cc of row becomes 1.
Done.

// Stamp a text pattern ("#" = alive) with its top-left corner at (top, left).
Bind void to stamp, given (the series of series of number board, the series of text pattern,
                           the number top, the number left,
                           the number height, the number width):
    Define pr as 0.
    For each line in pattern, repeat:
        Define line-len as the length of line.
        Define pc as 1.
        While pc is less than line-len + 1, repeat:
            Define ch as the characters from pc to pc of line.
            If ch is "#":
                Cast set-cell on (board, top + pr, left + pc - 1, height, width).
            Done.
            The pc becomes pc + 1.
        Done.
        The pr becomes pr + 1.
    Done.
Done.

Bind number to count-neighbors, given (the series of series of number board,
                                       the number r, the number c,
                                       the number height, the number width):
    Define total as 0.
    For each dr in range 0 - 1 to 1, repeat:
        For each dc in range 0 - 1 to 1, repeat:
            If dr is 0 and dc is 0, skip.
            Define rr as cast wrap-index on (r + dr, height).
            Define cc as cast wrap-index on (c + dc, width).
            Define nrow as item rr of board.
            Define v as item cc of nrow.
            The total becomes total + v.
        Done.
    Done.
    Return total.
Done.

Bind series of series of number to next-board, given (the series of series of number board,
                                                      the number height, the number width):
    Define next as cast make-board on (height, width).
    For each r in range 1 to height, repeat:
        Define row as item r of board.
        Define next-row as item r of next.
        For each c in range 1 to width, repeat:
            Define alive as item c of row.
            Define n as cast count-neighbors on (board, r, c, height, width).
            If alive is 1:
                If n is 2 or n is 3:
                    The item c of next-row becomes 1.
                Done.
            Done.
            Otherwise:
                If n is 3:
                    The item c of next-row becomes 1.
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
    Done.
    Return next.
Done.

Bind void to render, given (the series of series of number board,
                            the number height, the number width):
    For each r in range 1 to height, repeat:
        Define row as item r of board.
        Define line as "".
        For each c in range 1 to width, repeat:
            Define cell as item c of row.
            If cell is 1:
                The line becomes line joined to "#".
            Done.
            Otherwise:
                The line becomes line joined to ".".
            Done.
        Done.
        State line.
    Done.
Done.

Bind void to play:
    Define height as 16.
    Define width as 32.
    Define board as cast make-board on (height, width).

    Define glider as a series of text with (
        ".#.",
        "..#",
        "###").

    Define pulsar as a series of text with (
        "..###...###..",
        ".............",
        "#....#.#....#",
        "#....#.#....#",
        "#....#.#....#",
        "..###...###..",
        ".............",
        "..###...###..",
        "#....#.#....#",
        "#....#.#....#",
        "#....#.#....#",
        ".............",
        "..###...###..").

    Cast stamp on (board, pulsar, 2, 2, height, width).
    Cast stamp on (board, glider, 2, 20, height, width).
    Cast stamp on (board, glider, 12, 28, height, width).

    Define gens as 24.
    Define g as 0.
    While g is less than gens, repeat:
        State "Generation " joined to g converted to text.
        Cast render on (board, height, width).
        State "".
        The board becomes cast next-board on (board, height, width).
        The g becomes g + 1.
    Done.
Done.

Cast play.